From 956ee2d681f2d00ade99a1ff909ab8bd7b599cda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:26:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GBM] COwnScanout: buffers of 8 bits, and linear where
 they are asked to be

Kodi's own scanout buffers (COwnScanout) were made for output of more
than 8 bits only: 10-bit and half-float formats, checked with values that
8 bits cannot hold. An HDMI 3D frame-packed mode of nvidia-drm needs
buffers of 8 bits of Kodi's own, of the format of the window (issue #33,
the next commits), whose lines lie one after another.

- Bits() and Supported() take the four 8-bit RGB formats of a window
  (AR24, XR24, AB24, XB24): 8.
- Probe() and FlipProbe() take the depth of the buffer: a buffer of 8
  bits is cleared to 8-bit codes, distinct per component, and read back
  as bytes, each of which has to come back as it was written. A buffer
  that does not keep 8-bit values (RGB565) fails, and says why. 10 bits
  and half floats are checked as before.
- The framebuffer that a frame is drawn into before the GPU flips it is
  RGBA8 for buffers of 8 bits.
- Create() takes "linear": where GBM makes the buffers without
  modifiers, it is told GBM_BO_USE_LINEAR. The buffers of more than 8
  bits are made as before (not linear).
- BufferAt(): each buffer, for a test of each before anything is shown
  through them.

The output of more than 8 bits does not change: the same formats are
chosen for it (Bits() == 10, IsFloat()), with the same checks and flags.
